{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle","id":246616,"title":"The Huntsman Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-01T21:24:23-07:00","id":246616,"title":"The Huntsman Chronicle","content":"From the What's New section from Gen Con, they had in their list that the chronicle for Lost 2E is called the Huntsman Chronicle. To me, this tells me that The Wild Hunt might be more active in the game from a metaplot point. What's your thoughts about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T21:27:55-07:00","id":246632,"title":"","content":"You're late to the party. Check out the Changeling 2nd Edition threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T21:53:28-07:00","id":246642,"title":"","content":"Also, there is <i>still</i> no metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T22:04:57-07:00","id":246645,"title":"","content":"Also, Huntsmen can mean a lot of things. Certainly the terror of <i>a </i>Wild Hunt is a potent thing(And it is <i>a </i> Wild Hunt, since that's what hunting parties of Strangers are), but a privateer or loyalist or goblin looking for folks to sell or humans who see a scam in the works are <i>all</i> Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> The people who go looking for Changelings-those are the story catalysts. Wild Hunts are just the worst of those, and the game certainly wasn't called Too Solid Flesh: The Wild Hunt Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T01:26:42-07:00","id":246700,"title":"","content":"I certainly hope there's a focus on Privateers and Loyalists. I always thought the paranoia within Changeling culture was one of the more interesting social attributes of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T01:38:16-07:00","id":247633,"title":"","content":"Here's how David explained it to me, and I'm paraphrasing:<br /> <br /> Think of the Huntsmen as anything that wants to take you Back. Wild Hunts, Loyalists, Privateers, Goblins, whatever.<br /> <br /> They dominate your life from then on. Not just in their physical presence, but your mental presence.<br /> <br /> That guy looks at you weird for too long? Did he notice your horns? Does he know?<br /> <br /> The elevator's taking too long. Has someone stopped it to capture you?<br /> <br /> The idea that Changeling is a game about abuse survivors that are trying (keyword &quot;trying&quot;) to move on with their lives is an old one. But it's a good one, and it's the one we're focusing on.<br /> <br /> That's the Huntsmen Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T10:48:54-07:00","id":248001,"title":"","content":"Is Talecrafting going to be part of the core book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T23:46:38-07:00","id":248664,"title":"","content":"God I hope not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:46:06-07:00","id":248844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=248664#post248664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God I hope not.</div> </div> </div> </div>People being malicious and misrepresentative about what the ability actually did has no bearing on whether or not it ought to be included under the assumption that it would be properly implemented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T09:17:53-07:00","id":248902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=248001#post248001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Talecrafting going to be part of the core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only hope.<br /> <br /> The concept was good, it just had too many strictures on it, based as it was on the idea that player agency=bad.<br /> <br /> An understandable position in a horror game, but at some point it just...gets...boring. The fact you couldn't shake the addiction in play too didn't help.<br /> <br /> Just make the addiction a Condition that can be helped in-chronicle without massive boredom, and that solves 60% of my problem right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T09:53:29-07:00","id":248942,"title":"","content":"I quite love Talecrafting and would love to see it in the book.<br /> <br /> I'm just not sure it has a place in there. It might pull too much away from the strong thematic direction for readers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:33:50-07:00","id":248963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=248844#post248844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People being malicious and misrepresentative about what the ability actually did has no bearing on whether or not it ought to be included under the assumption that it would be properly implemented.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) what does/did it actually do?<br /> <br /> B) a'course, new edition, no proof it'll resemble old talecrafting when they are done, so maybe A should be 'supposed to do'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:45:12-07:00","id":248966,"title":"","content":"Talecrafting should be a dangerous thing to, in that incentivizes characters and players to fall into patterns of perception and behavior that defines them and the world on arbitrary roles provided by narrative fate for benefit. In short, it should evoke the idea of putting on the same sort of yoke the Strangers put on the PC's to begin with, or worse incentivizing them to act like the Strangers. Going with the survivor metaphor, it's a person's tendency to fall back into the old (bad) habits of their survival experience* for ease.<br /> <br /> Many people interpret Talecrafting instead as &quot;Leaning on the fourth wall LOL tvtropesismiengreatarsenal&quot;.<br /> <br /> *I'm starting to see what Dave meant when he said it's about survivors, not necessarily those of abuse. Having never played it, the ideas that went into the last Tomb Raider are still a good notation for Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-04-2014, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:56:33-07:00","id":248976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=248963#post248963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A) what does/did it actually do?<br /> <br /> B) a'course, new edition, no proof it'll resemble old talecrafting when they are done, so maybe A should be 'supposed to do'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Talecrafting gives players a way to &quot;take&quot; narrative control away from the GM and edit the environment to their benefit as long as the changes adhere to a fairy tale motif. Doing it too often was really bad for Clarity. The system was a little weird to incorporate given that the Changeling already had a ton of mini-games and Talecrafting is one of the more complicated ones.<br /> <br /> I think the idea is cool ... but with Pledgecrafting, Hedgespinning, Onieromancy, Contracts ... it is just way too many things. It would be great if Talecrafting could be folded in with something else, like maybe Pledges or Onieromancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T18:45:20-07:00","id":249359,"title":"","content":"I like the original idea behind talecrafting, the story theme for the powers worked well with the game's tendency for dark whimsy and when I first read it I thought it was really cool. I think the original idea might have been to give players the option to do some more flexable, fae-like magic similar to the desire more than a few people have expressed for wyrd sorcery. From that angle I understand it and even kind of like it but\u2026 yeah it got a bit weird with some of the stuff it did (I'm going to dig a random hole and there's going to be treasure in it!). Were I writing it I'd work it similar to a pledge (one sided, treat the endeavor as a boon that will be fulfilled as long as you play the &quot;role&quot; that you're meant to have in the story) but it probably deserves a more thorough system if it is used. Much as I enjoy the concept of talecrafting I think it might be better left for something after the core book, if it shows up at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:20:14-07:00","id":249387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=248966#post248966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talecrafting should be a dangerous thing to, in that incentivizes characters and players to fall into patterns of perception and behavior that defines them and the world on arbitrary roles provided by narrative fate for benefit. In short, it should evoke the idea of putting on the same sort of yoke the Strangers put on the PC's to begin with, or worse incentivizing them to act like the Strangers. Going with the survivor metaphor, it's a person's tendency to fall back into the old (bad) habits of their survival experience* for ease.<br /> <br /> Many people interpret Talecrafting instead as &quot;Leaning on the fourth wall LOL tvtropesismiengreatarsenal&quot;.<br /> <br /> *I'm starting to see what Dave meant when he said it's about survivors, not necessarily those of abuse. Having never played it, the ideas that went into the last Tomb Raider are still a good notation for Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh my god. If you look at that from the perspective of a Changeling escaping the Hedge, it becomes something entirely different. I mentioned this in a backstage discussion, but (minor spoiler) the underground caverns filled with bodies and blood? That's in Lara's mind. There's no realistic way there could be THAT many bodies down there. That's what it looks like when your Clarity gets challenged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:44:25-07:00","id":249398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=249387#post249387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh my god. If you look at that from the perspective of a Changeling escaping the Hedge, it becomes something entirely different. I mentioned this in a backstage discussion, but (minor spoiler) the underground caverns filled with bodies and blood? That's in Lara's mind. There's no realistic way there could be THAT many bodies down there. That's what it looks like when your Clarity gets challenged.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started thinking about that after I put that, actually.(I haven't played it because, protip, never play Tomb Raider on PC without a controller, but I have watched other play it in my apartment) Lara's not exactly the most reliable narrator after all,so the entire game, with it's theme of survival, really does become this eerie sort of analog.<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder just how unreliable she actually is...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Could a really <i>bad</i> Clarity drop result in a need to navigate your nightmares, ala the caverns or even akin to American McGee's Alice or the Dream levels of Max Payne, something akin to the Death Cycle from Mummy?<br /> <br /> EDIT: That might make a cool optional rule in the storytelling chapter, if Blood Smoke's use of those represents a consistent book design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-04-2014, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:51:04-07:00","id":249442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=249398#post249398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started thinking about that after I put that, actually.(I haven't played it because, protip, never play Tomb Raider on PC without a controller, but I have watched other play it in my apartment) Lara's not exactly the most reliable narrator after all,so the entire game, with it's theme of survival, really does become this eerie sort of analog.<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder just how unreliable she actually is...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Could a really <i>bad</i> Clarity drop result in a need to navigate your nightmares, ala the caverns or even akin to American McGee's Alice or the Dream levels of Max Payne, something akin to the Death Cycle from Mummy?<br /> <br /> EDIT: That might make a cool optional rule in the storytelling chapter, if Blood Smoke's use of those represents a consistent book design.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those Storytelling sections will exist in Mage, Werewolf, like they did in Vampire. Those are all Filamena and me. I can't speak to what Stew is doing in Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T03:38:36-07:00","id":249673,"title":"","content":"Everything I've heard about this Chronicle makes me more interested. Which is probably good, because nChangeling is definitely my favorite line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=249398#post249398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started thinking about that after I put that, actually.(I haven't played it because, protip, never play Tomb Raider on PC without a controller, but I have watched other play it in my apartment) Lara's not exactly the most reliable narrator after all,so the entire game, with it's theme of survival, really does become this eerie sort of analog.<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder just how unreliable she actually is...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but Tomb Raider 2013 is actually about a queer college student entering the patriarchal professional world and utterly destroying it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","user":"Illuminated Minutia","date":". 09-05-2014, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T10:36:30-07:00","id":249935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=249673#post249673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but Tomb Raider 2013 is actually about a queer college student entering the patriarchal professional world and utterly destroying it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It can be about that too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T11:35:04-07:00","id":253502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/246616-the-huntsman-chronicle?p=249359#post249359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the original idea behind talecrafting, the story theme for the powers worked well with the game's tendency for dark whimsy and when I first read it I thought it was really cool. I think the original idea might have been to give players the option to do some more flexable, fae-like magic similar to the desire more than a few people have expressed for wyrd sorcery. From that angle I understand it and even kind of like it but\u2026 yeah it got a bit weird with some of the stuff it did (I'm going to dig a random hole and there's going to be treasure in it!). Were I writing it I'd work it similar to a pledge (one sided, treat the endeavor as a boon that will be fulfilled as long as you play the &quot;role&quot; that you're meant to have in the story) but it probably deserves a more thorough system if it is used. Much as I enjoy the concept of talecrafting I think it might be better left for something after the core book, if it shows up at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were I writing it, &quot;it&quot; would simply be a set of Contracts that resemble and, to an extent, enforce various tropes from folklore. You know, like Contracts are already designed to do, hopefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T15:28:03-07:00","id":259303,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Talecrafting should be placed on the higher end of the Wyrd scale? Something a changeling finds themselves able to do around the same time their mask becomes unreliable and they develop little folkloric allergens to things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}